# fused-linear-fallback.diff — exl3_plain v1: fused SGLang linears take the sanctioned dequant->BF16 path.
#
# Gate-2 failure (2384, image :serve sha256:a10d5012, 2026-09-13 06:16 UTC):
#   ValueError: model.language_model.layers.0.self_attn.qkv_proj: fused SGLang linear cannot take a
#   native trellis payload        (linear.py:50, Exl3LinearMethod.create_weights, output_partition_sizes=3)
# Cause: config.get_quant_method chose Exl3LinearMethod from the census verdict alone
# (dense_sparkinfer_native = kernel-capable); QKVParallelLinear owns one weight for q/k/v and
# loads by shard, which a native trellis payload cannot do.  Two further latent failures of the same
# shape were found while tracing: (1) q_a_proj / kv_a_proj_with_mqa are census-native but SGLang
# concatenates them into fused_qkv_a_proj_with_mqa, so the loader would raise "EXL3 dense target
# missing"; (2) vision prefixes ("visual.x") never mapped to their census module ("model.visual.x"),
# so vision attn.proj / mlp.down_proj / merger.* would have hit the same missing-target error.
#
# Change (config.py, loader.py, linear.py; dequant.py unchanged):
#   * get_quant_method: a native-capable source whose SGLang consumer is FUSED (len(layer.output_sizes) > 1,
#     the same predicate ColumnParallelLinear uses; set before LinearBase.__init__ by QKVParallelLinear and
#     MergedColumnParallelLinear) is ANNOUNCED once per (SGLang class <- source class) and routed to
#     UnquantizedLinearMethod; the config records it in fallback_bound.  Unfused consumers bind
#     Exl3LinearMethod and are recorded in native_bound (source -> SGLang prefix).
#   * loader: routes by config.native_bound (what was actually constructed), not by the census verdict;
#     everything else DENSE takes the sanctioned dequant path with the reason in the per-class log line;
#     byte accounting unchanged (resident = N*K*2 per dequantized module; every tensor in one row).
#   * source_module: adds the "visual." -> "model.visual." candidate so unfused vision modules stay native.
#   * linear.py: fused check kept as an unreachable routing-bug guard; message says so.
# Result on the 2.05 mul1 artifact: native trellis = o_proj x46, q_b_proj x12, indexer.wq_b x12,
# mlp.down_proj x3, shared_experts.down_proj x43, lm_head, vision attn.proj x24, vision mlp.down_proj x24,
# merger.proj, merger.down_proj.  Dequant->BF16 = qkv_proj x34, q_a_proj x12, kv_a_proj_with_mqa x12,
# mlp.gate/up_proj x3+3, shared_experts.gate/up_proj x43+43, vision mlp.gate/up x24+24, merger gate/up.
# Verified: py_compile; stub-routing test over the real census receipt (14 SGLang module cases, 16-module
# synthetic load stream, byte report printed).  NOT yet run on GPU.
# Apply (after contract-widen.diff and moe-mul1-marker.diff; no overlapping hunks):
#   cd <dir containing exl3_plain_sglang_overlay/> && patch -p1 -i fused-linear-fallback.diff
diff --color -ru a/exl3_plain_sglang_overlay/config.py b/exl3_plain_sglang_overlay/config.py
--- a/exl3_plain_sglang_overlay/config.py	2026-09-13 02:22:38
